  [skill] Monthly cross-sectional IC: mean +0.032, std 0.169, t-stat +1.16. Annualized IR: +0.66 — strong (>0.5 is institutionally meaningful). Pooled IC across all observations: -0.013. Interpretation: the cross-sectional rank correlation is positive on average — the score discriminates winners from losers in the same period.

  [quintiles] Mean forward return by score quintile (Q1=lowest score → Q5=highest): Q1=+1.23% (n=523), Q2=+1.03% (n=522), Q3=+0.98% (n=522), Q4=+0.66% (n=522), Q5=+1.06% (n=523)

  [portfolio] Equal-weight long-top-quintile / short-bottom-quintile portfolio, rebalanced every 21 trading days: mean per-period return +0.93%, summed across the window +34.50%. This is a simple sum, not a compounded total — it isolates the per-rebalance edge before transaction costs, financing, and slippage.

  [universe] Point-in-time universe applied: 89 observation(s) were dropped because the ticker was not an index member on that date. 73 names contributed at least one scored month.

